 r←RefreshData arg;new
⍝ When triggered by ⎕WC timer, argument is the timer object
⍝ When called via HTTP request, argument is request object
⍝ Argument not used in either case
 :If '⍠SPEC'≡arg
     r←(
         tags:,⊂'Admin' ⋄ summary:'Refresh cached API data' ⋄ operationId:'refreshData'
         description:'Fetches external API data, then rebuilds the cached joined views served by the public read endpoints.'
     )
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :Trap 202 404
     ##.IMPORT.YOUTUBE.RefreshData''
 :Else
     ⎕←'DATA NOT REFRESHED. ',⎕DMX.Message
 :EndTrap
 ⍙CACHE←#.ø #.DCMS.CACHE       ⍝ Spawn isolate to build cache in separate process
 'new'⎕NS ⍙CACHE.Build(        ⍝ Build new cache in isolate. Does not block threads in main process despite waiting for future to resolve.
     using:##.⎕USING           ⍝ Must deep clone 'new'⎕NS ref because result ref from namespace-returning isolate cannot be dotted into (interpreter bug)
     app_dir:##.app_dir
 )
 :Hold '#.DCMS.GLOBAL.cache'   ⍝ One-shot update is safe across threads. Readers take snapshots to get complete cache view.
     #.DCMS.GLOBAL.cache←new
     #.DCMS.GLOBAL.cache.videos.(Lookup←index∘⍳)
 :EndHold
 ⎕←r←'Refreshed data at ',⍕⎕TS
